==English==

===Etymology===
{{compound|en|split|end}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# A [[hair]] which has [[split]] at the [[end]], usually from [[dryness]] or [[poor]] [[nutrition]].
#: {{ux|en|I've got so many '''split ends''' – I think I must be working too hard.}}
# {{lb|en|in the plural}} The condition of having [[hair]]s with [[split]] [[end]]s.
#: {{synonyms|en|schizotrichia|trichoptilosis}}
#: {{ux|en|Help! I've got '''split ends'''!}}
# {{lb|en|American football}} The [[position]] which [[line up|lines up]] [[wide]] and on the [[offensive line of scrimmage]], whose primary job is to serve as a [[wide receiver]].
#: {{syn|en|wideout}}
#: {{ux|en|Jones played '''split end'''.}}
# {{lb|en|American football}} A [[player]] [[play]]ing the [[position]] of split end.
#: {{ux|en|The '''split end''' ran deep.}}

